omated voices of the conference  call system saying something like Peter  Droid to call Peter Rowe the coil Peter  join to call Peter Bob the caller right  so whenever somebody joins or drops the  call in many conference call systems  there's an automatic voice saying that  to all the people in the car and of  course if you've been there if you've  seen these kind of things  this is extremely disturbing because if  somebody joins or drops the call  basically the conversation is  interrupted by their voice so how can  you diminish this disturbance as much as  possible when and again this very much  also depends on the conference call  system that you're using how exactly  that works but frequently whenever you  dial into a conference call the system  often asks you for your name so it will  say something like please tell us your  name after the beep sound and then press  the hash button right so it asks you to  say your name and then press the button  usually the hash key so that the system  knows that now the recording can stop  your name so what you need to do where  the little trick is that when you're  being asked to tell your name just don't  tell your name just don't say anything  and directly press the hash key so it  asks you and you directly press it  without any second left so that it  cannot really record anything and then  when you join or when you drop the call  there will just be no sound of the  system saying your name for everybody  because this recording of the name just  that exists so whenever the system asks  you for your name press the hash key  don't say your name and you will be fine  of course if there's a strict rule in  your company that you need to say your  name well then do that don't get a  trouble for that but most companies  there isn't anything like that and I can  tell you if you do this and if you tell  or your co-workers to do this your  conference calls will go much more  smoothly because this kind of  disturbance just isn't there anymore so  guys my third tip is about what to do  when you actually join the conference  call late and of course this can happen  for all kinds of reasons but what many  people do which I find quite  disrespectful and disturbing is the  person's late the discussion is already  ongoing  and then the person joins to call and  then just says something like hi guys hi  yeah I'm late sorry for that I was just  stuck in traffic but now I'm here sorry  for that right and by doing that he  disrupts he interrupts the whole  conversation and just stops the person  who is currently doing and especially a  large conference calls where there many  people online in the car and many people  come in late with all these people then  apologize for being late and then in the  worst case even also different reason  why they were late this is just such a  disturbance so from my experience the  best practice radius if you are joining  the conference call and you are late  just say nothing don't introduce  yourself that you are there now don't  apologize why you are late just say  nothing and this is especially true if  you can hear that the car already  started and there's already a  conversation going on and of course that  might be different if you are the CEO of  the company or you are the person is  actually supposed to lead the whole  conference call is the most important  person in the coil then maybe it's okay  and then it may make sense that you let  all the others know that you are there  but if you are just one of many  participants most likely the others  really not really care if you are there  or not or at least they won't care as  much for you to interrupt the whole  discussion just for letting in the know  so just be quiet and just use the next  opportunity where you see a moment when  you can just add something meaningful to  the discussion but you can say that and  then also by doing the letting let us  know that now you join the chorus may  the fourth tip on conference cards is to  be concise so for all these reasons and  many others conference cards can be  quite tiresome and annoying everybody  should contribute for making these cards  as short and as efficient as possible  and we all know these people who just in  meetings and conversations need to have  the stage time these people that feel  like that they always need to say  something that even though that has been  already said many times they need to  repeat  again people that state the obvious just  to say something this is annoying and  this is not only annoying conference  calls but of course also in regular  meetings as well but this is especially  annoying conference cards because  conference cards in itself often our a  bit of an annoying situation and this  only makes it worse so make sure that  when you say something it really adds  venue to the conversation  you're not just repeating things that  others have already said you are not  stating the obvious so things that are  completely obvious but you just say them  just because you feel like need to say  something do not do these things beep on  sighs for the sake of everybody involved  and now my fifth tip is if any how  possible only join the call if you have  a more or less stable connection I mean  also we've all been in these situations  where are people joined from an airport  maybe already sitting in an airplane or  they join from the car or they join from  the train and then they constantly lose  the connection drop off the car then  drop in again and this is just the  disturbance because even if you do not  say your name at the beginning so it  doesn't always say Peter joined or left  the call often does that these the  beeping sound which is the disturbance  so if you already know that you will not  have a stable connection for your  telephone conference and if there's any  way for you that maybe your attendance  isn't absolutely crucial or maybe  there's a way to postpone into a moment  may actually have a more stable  connection do not join if your  connection is unstable because again it  is a big disturbance to all the other  people on the call it is annoying and  it's a waste of time so be respectful to  the time of your co-workers so these  were my five tips and of course I'm  interested not to hear how is your work  environment changing these dire times in  this global pandemic is it true for you  as well  that you're not having many more  conference calls let me know what your  experience is below in the comments I'd  love to hear from you  and if you have any other tips that  you'd like to share with our community  here on firm learning let us know I'm  sure that others would appreciate as  well  what are your do's and don'ts for having  good and effective telephone conferences  and of course if you took any value out  of this video at all if always please  press the like button to help the  YouTube algorithm that other people find  this video as well and if you'd like to  see more videos on how you can be  successful in the first years of your  career videos similar like this please  press the subscribe button of course  I'd also love to hear your feedback  topics you'd like to see covered in this  channel just let me know and I include  this on my list of ideas for the future  videos I will release at least one video  every week so thank you for hanging in  here with me thank you for joining thank  you for watching my name is Haile from  firm learning stay safe everybody and  have a good day

